def render(context):
    exec(compile('st.header(\n    "About EVChargeIQ"\n)\nst.markdown(\n    """\n    ### Problem Statement\n\n    EV adoption and charging infrastructure expansion vary\n    across Indian states. EVChargeIQ analyzes historical\n    OMC-reported charging infrastructure data, compares\n    state-level patterns, and evaluates machine-learning\n    models for estimating subsequent-year infrastructure\n    installations.\n\n    ### Primary Datasets\n\n    **Charging Infrastructure**\n\n    Ministry of Heavy Industries, Government of India.\n\n    Public Information Bureau release dated 27 March 2026.\n\n    The dataset includes state-wise annual OMC charger\n    installation figures, installed totals and operational\n    charger counts. FY 2025-26 figures are partial through\n    1 March 2026.\n\n    **EV Registrations**\n\n    VAHAN public vehicle registration data, processed\n    into a state-wise annual EV registration dataset.\n\n    ### Data Science Workflow\n\n    1. Data collection\n    2. Data validation\n    3. Data cleaning\n    4. Data transformation\n    5. Exploratory data analysis\n    6. Feature engineering\n    7. Regression modelling\n    8. Model evaluation\n    9. Interactive visualization\n\n    ### Machine Learning Algorithms\n\n    - Linear Regression\n    - Decision Tree Regressor\n    - Random Forest Regressor\n\n    ### Evaluation Metrics\n\n    - Mean Absolute Error (MAE)\n    - Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)\n    - R-squared (R²)\n\n    ### Technology Stack\n\n    - Python\n    - Pandas\n    - NumPy\n    - Scikit-learn\n    - Plotly\n    - Streamlit\n\n    ### Limitations\n\n    - The infrastructure dataset uses OMC-reported data,\n      not a complete inventory of all public charging operators.\n    - FY 2025-26 infrastructure data is partial.\n    - The model uses a limited number of state-year observations.\n    - Annual EV registrations are not cumulative active EV stock.\n    - State-wise registration pressure is an exploratory\n      indicator, not a verified measure of infrastructure shortage.\n    - Model estimates are exploratory and are not official forecasts.\n    """\n)\nst.subheader(\n    "Data Sources"\n)\nst.markdown(\n    "[Official PIB / Ministry of Heavy Industries source]"\n    "(https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2246042)"\n)\nst.markdown(\n    "[VAHAN Public Dashboard]"\n    "(https://www.analytics.parivahan.gov.in/analytics/publicdashboard/vahan)"\n)\nst.markdown(\n    "[NITI Aayog India Electric Mobility Index]"\n    "(https://www.niti.gov.in/node/2424)"\n)\nst.divider()\nst.caption(\n    "EVChargeIQ | MCA Data Science Project | 2026 | "\n    "Exploratory Academic Prototype"\n)', __file__, 'exec'), context)
